<title>USA: Fed adds permanent reserves via coupon pass.</title>
<headline>Fed adds permanent reserves via coupon pass.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added permanent reserves to the U.S. banking system on Tuesday via a coupon pass, a Fed spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The Fed bought coupons from May 15, 2002 to February 15, 2007 for delivery on Wednesday, the spokeswoman added.</p>
<p>U.S. economists had expected a permanent injection of reserves. The move follows another purchase of coupons carried out by the Fed roughly 10 days ago.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
